{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1519984-curse-when-a-fetch-is-in-league-with-their-changeling","id":1519984,"title":"Curse when a fetch is in league with their changeling...?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-06T14:10:37-07:00","id":1519984,"title":"Curse when a fetch is in league with their changeling...?","content":"My table has a character in it that has the merits &quot;<i>Touchstone</i>&quot;, &quot;<i>Ally</i>&quot;, &quot;<i>True Friend</i>&quot; and &quot;<i>Parallel Lives</i>&quot; all at the same time for the same person: her fetch. When the Changeling returned from her durance, her fetch adopted her as an identical twin sister (and vice-versa). Despite the two having a ton in common, both have separate names, separate senses of identities and selves, and even though they argue and make up over everything like a married couple in a romantic comedy soap opera they do so in a comparatively healthy way. If people in their usual social circles (including the Changeling's Freehold) sees one without the other, sometimes people ask questions so reintegrating is off the table for the both of them.<br /> <br /> However, several months in, I gathered that apparently we're not actually supposed to be doing this, and that Fetches that try to reconcile with their Changelings or help their Changeling find a place in life alongside them suffer a type of curse. If this is intended to be structural to the game, I've not actually come across that in the core rulebook at this point in time.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any further sources on where I could read more on this? I don't have many of the books for First Edition, but it's my understanding that First Edition had some stuff that hasn't yet been brought forward, but could be easily modernized to work with the Second, and is still intended to be a part of the same continuity and the same worldbuilding.<br /> <br /> Outside of the books, any of your own thoughts or opinions on a situation like this are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Project to convert Chronicles of Darkness to a data-driven <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1499154-homebrew-vehicular-and-combined-arms-combat-in-cofd\" target=\"_blank\">Combined Arms Simulation: Gods of Iron</a><br /> My personal website, projects and games: <a href=\"https://puckerfactorgames.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://puckerfactorgames.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27707-jester-pfg","name":"Jester-PFG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27707_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T14:36:57-07:00","id":1519986,"title":"","content":"In first edition, a changeling coming to terms with a Fetch was considered a storytelling option. Granted, it wasn't supposed to be an easy option; just approaching the fetch and revealing to them what they were would complicate things considerably.<br /> <br /> I don't know anything about a curse, but my (likely flawed) understanding is that becoming allied or befriending your fetch is something best played out in the chronicle, not neatly taken care of in the backstory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T17:00:45-07:00","id":1519996,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think they\u2019re anything like a general setting defining curse on befriending your Fetch\u2026just that most Changelings would view you as crazy for hanging out with a know tool of your Keeper. Like, maybe the Fetch really does want to be nice, and is open to an arrangement\u2026or maybe it\u2019s a trap programmed into it by your Keeper. The poor scarecrow probably wasn\u2019t even aware it wasn\u2019t you, what else could it be unaware of? It\u2019s know that *some* Changelings were only taken so that their keeper could have a servant iron side. Basically, I expect many Changelings to be both reasonably and not so reasonably skeptical of befriending a Fetch. Maybe several previous attempts went bad, and people started talking about a curse. Maybe there really is something to the rumors, and maybe people are just seeing things in an extremely difficult task. Maybe it\u2019s intentional fear mongering from one of the courts, or one of the more aware Fetches or one of the Fetch adjacent beings hanging out in mirror space.<br /> <br /> Of course, one might note that merging with each other could be seen as curse from the Fetches perspective. After all, the being that remains afterward bears the most resemblance to the Changeling. Maybe one of the Gentry was being \u201ctruthful\u201d when a Fetch/Hob/Changeling asked about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T20:10:51-07:00","id":1520010,"title":"","content":"Hey, thanks for the thoughts, Father Enoch and TempleBuilder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Project to convert Chronicles of Darkness to a data-driven <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1499154-homebrew-vehicular-and-combined-arms-combat-in-cofd\" target=\"_blank\">Combined Arms Simulation: Gods of Iron</a><br /> My personal website, projects and games: <a href=\"https://puckerfactorgames.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://puckerfactorgames.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27707-jester-pfg","name":"Jester-PFG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27707_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T10:38:10-07:00","id":1520221,"title":"","content":"I haven't heard anything about a &quot;curse&quot; for a Changeling and their Fetch getting along. Considering that the book has notes about Fetch potentially becoming members of a Freehold, and outright stating a Fetch could be a Changeling's Touchstone, it seems unlikely such a thing is in 2e proper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T12:10:06-07:00","id":1520229,"title":"","content":"Wasn't there an example Fetch who realized what he was, and resolved to had over their life to the Changeling as soon as he found them? Was a chef, I think. That might have been a 1e thing though","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T14:06:24-07:00","id":1520235,"title":"","content":"<br /> Hey, also thank you for the thoughts Cauthon and Taidragon!<br /> <br /> I'll go and see if I can find the part about that, I could go and buy the 1st Edition Books for CTL. Since I haven't really run this before nor had it been run, having reference examples, published adventure modules and characters I can refer back to is extremely valuable for me because it's a good way I can learn what to expect or how the developers intended the game to be played, even if I never use them and never use their stats.<br /> <br /> Although this sounds like the Changeling and Fetch working together should be something of an exception and not the rule, I was trying to think about other ways that the Fetch and Changeling dynamic could be used to provide some greater variety and shake things up a bit, so as to allow for greater variation in my PCs' respective experiences. Not all duos should immediately welcome each other with open arms, go about building healthy relationships and becoming fire-forged friends and share their lives together, but I figured it would get a bit samey if Fetches were universally compelled to always try to make enemies out of someone with a lot of faerie power.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Project to convert Chronicles of Darkness to a data-driven <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1499154-homebrew-vehicular-and-combined-arms-combat-in-cofd\" target=\"_blank\">Combined Arms Simulation: Gods of Iron</a><br /> My personal website, projects and games: <a href=\"https://puckerfactorgames.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://puckerfactorgames.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27707-jester-pfg","name":"Jester-PFG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27707_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-20T19:03:13-07:00","id":1521090,"title":"","content":"There's not a curse preventing a Changeling becoming close with their fetch, but I can think of a few things that someone might have half remembered as indicating it. Breaking a pledge sworn on your true name (in 1e) gives your fetch significant power to harm you. One of the books features chapter heading fiction where a Changeling gets beaten half to death by his freehold for befriending his fetch, and the fetch is dying of cancer. Tragic, but not symptomatic of a wider curse.<br /> There's another character in one of the later books who employs his fetch as manservant and confidant, and they are successful if not especially nice. In general there are plenty of examples of fetches and changelings who are not necessarily antagonistic toward each other, although vanishingly few examples of relationships that are both happy and healthy.<br /> Truthfully the real curse is being in a Chronicles game, where healthy relationships aren't allowed lest it ruin the drama. (I jest. Mostly.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}